exports[`renderAgentContext > renders the whole AGENTS.md block 1`] = `
"<!-- coreloom-uml:begin · managed block, edits inside it are replaced on the next pull -->
## Project

This repository is **Shop**: Online shop for \\*rare\\* books

Its architectures, as described in Coreloom UML:

- **Orders**: Order taking and payment
  - Order model (class diagram)
  - Checkout (sequence diagram)
- **Catalog**.

## Working style

- Comment only to explain why; never restate what the code does.

## TypeScript

- Never use \`any\`; prefer \`unknown\` with narrowing or an explicit type.
- The code base is TypeScript \`strict\`: never loosen compiler options or silence errors with \`@ts-ignore\`.

## React

- Keep components small and focused; extract a component as soon as a part has its own state or responsibility.
- Server state lives in TanStack Query; keep other state local to components and add no state library.
- Style with Tailwind utility classes; do not add CSS files or inline styles.
- Prefer \\\`useSuspenseQuery\\\` in routes.

## Testing

- Add or update unit tests for every change in logic.
- Add or update an end-to-end test when a user journey changes.

## Workflow

- Ask before any structural decision (new dependency, new pattern, data model or public API change).

## Tooling

- Use pnpm for every install and script; never another package manager.
- Before handing back, run: pnpm lint && pnpm test.

## Project notes

The notes below were written by the project owner.

Deploys go through **staging** first.

\\<script>alert(1)\\</script>
<!-- coreloom-uml:end -->
"
`;
